WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.031
Imagine four business teams with four
promising AI proposals.

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:08.040
Each seems manageable. But all need the
same operational experts

00:00:08.045 --> 00:00:11.880
to check outputs, handle exceptions and
approve new workflows.

00:00:11.885 --> 00:00:14.173
Those experts still have day jobs.

00:00:14.178 --> 00:00:17.100
The projects are approved; the capacity
isn't.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.745
I've worked across enterprise AI
delivery and the assessment of

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.705
competing AI initiatives. An inventory
shows leadership what's underway.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:30.220
It doesn't show what the business can
finish.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.811
I distinguish three capacities. Decision
capacity:

00:00:32.816 --> 00:00:35.898
can leaders compare requests and stop or
redirect work?

00:00:35.903 --> 00:00:39.634
Delivery capacity: have the right
specialists been given actual time?

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:43.173
Operating capacity: can the business
support the service when the

00:00:43.178 --> 00:00:44.420
project team leaves?

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.132
Before moving beyond a bounded
experiment, I'd ask the sponsor

00:00:49.137 --> 00:00:54.532
for five commitments: the intended
business outcome, the accountable owner,

00:00:54.537 --> 00:00:59.604
time released from other work, shared
dependencies, and the evidence

00:00:59.609 --> 00:01:03.180
that would justify more investment—or an
exit.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.442
That creates four portfolio choices:
proceed, defer, combine or redesign,

00:01:07.447 --> 00:01:10.647
or stop. A deferred idea isn't
necessarily a bad idea;

00:01:10.652 --> 00:01:14.200
it may be more than the organization can
support today.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.854
At the next review, put active AI
initiatives beside the

00:01:17.859 --> 00:01:21.330
people they depend on. For each new
priority, ask what

00:01:21.335 --> 00:01:25.364
existing work will give way. Without a
credible answer, leadership

00:01:25.369 --> 00:01:28.800
has approved an intention, not a
deliverable commitment.

